    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0438" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg330"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you,
                    herewith, for the use of Her Britannic Majesty’s Government twelve copies of the
                    President’s proclamation of the 21st instant, declaring that until further
                    notice the provisions <pb facs="0439" n="331" xml:id="pg331"/> of his
                    proclamation of August 18, 1892, are suspended in so far as they direct that a
                    toll of 20 cents per ton be levied, collected, and paid on all freight of
                    whatever kind or description passing through the St. Mary’s Falls Canal in
                    transit to any port of the Dominion of Canada, whether carried in vessels of the
                    United States or of other nations.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d326-a1.xml" xpointer="d326-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
